{"title":"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A lattice point in an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate system is any point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> where both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are integers. The graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/2/1d2264e4e7d4e433b38289ec6dd77ddeb0a18f84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = mx + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> passes through no lattice point with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f17264b2875c57d6725ca2bad50be5250b19866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x \\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8ab24211e8c6cd92bef80e95ecf7d45d23afcc10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} &lt; m &lt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" />. What is the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5f173f9dafbf807595b2377a8bfa4adc76ffff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{51}{101} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{50}{99} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{51}{100} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{52}{101} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{13}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"440\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is very easy to see that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe54585e0c171194b0e07cc59767d097999658cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> in the graph does not impact whether it passes through the lattice. \n</p><p>We need to make sure that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be in the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084079bf1d54500f3c59257a7ec3467932b72ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/3966fdcb1e67bbabbd3b87cb3ace13fa0bd02ec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le b\\le 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />. Otherwise, the graph <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffab7ab34ab1ae629edd3198607def46afabd1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y= mx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"11\" /> passes through the lattice point at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b35766a1f98740c053f6dd3d88cf9fdbf8b996.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. We only need to worry about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084079bf1d54500f3c59257a7ec3467932b72ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" /> very close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8a15199b504168316da808f961d4eca5b26d2ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n+1}{2n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"57\" height=\"40\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15e0b53a90aad498c9e7dcef17e201934c6b1252.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n+1}{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" /> will be the only case we need to worry about and we want the minimum of those, clearly for  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/3966fdcb1e67bbabbd3b87cb3ace13fa0bd02ec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le b\\le 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />, the smallest is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699b40301620472a97d6073256ff855fbd199130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, so answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/b/29be17e30c8039a13e7cb834a06a001b9bc8fca8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{50}{99} \\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"62\" height=\"48\" /> (In other words we are trying to find the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/f/4cf985e12044d03e6fbd761cb1fc4c0d28873b8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&gt;\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"38\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e62959646dbcc5beefe8c04fefdf5c67f8aedda0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\le 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in the first solution, we note that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe54585e0c171194b0e07cc59767d097999658cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> does not affect our answer. Thus, we can ignore it and consider an equivalent problem with the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8cab3b86d4a13c3cc3680c32aaa80cc854689e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = mx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p>A line with a slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> passes through (among other lattice points) the lattice point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/1/2813504d248553bfdfe4adad6a58b2642fc6bcf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(100,50)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. As the slope of the line increases from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, the first lattice point it hits is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62e4771356d67b2ec6c2aeb83357b00d0db21703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(99, 50)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, the slope of that line being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699b40301620472a97d6073256ff855fbd199130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> . So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in the first solution, we note that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe54585e0c171194b0e07cc59767d097999658cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> does not affect our answer. Thus, we can ignore it and consider an equivalent problem with the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8cab3b86d4a13c3cc3680c32aaa80cc854689e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = mx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p>We will start with the first answer choice. Notice how it is impossible for a line with slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d75d57e066a182bb360075f72a27bad12f01ed0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{51}{101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" /> to pass through a lattice point when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f17264b2875c57d6725ca2bad50be5250b19866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x \\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>However, if the slope is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699b40301620472a97d6073256ff855fbd199130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, then the line will pass through the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62e4771356d67b2ec6c2aeb83357b00d0db21703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(99, 50)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />. This sets the upper bound for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~xHypotenuse\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B\">2011 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017155700\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 305/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7555/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.774      1 -total\n 59.49%    7.599      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 38.77%    4.953      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9130:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017155700 and revision id 222176. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}